# Frontend conventions

## Structure

- Features: `frontend/src/features/<domain>/`
- API client: `frontend/src/lib/api.ts`
- Routes: `frontend/src/routes/AppRoutes.tsx`, paths in `lib/paths.ts`
- Session/RBAC: `SessionContext`, permission checks via `can('permission.code')`

## Patterns

- Load data in feature tabs; use `apiEnabled` guard when API offline
- Invite links: `${origin}/invite?invite=${encodeURIComponent(token)}` — never `/app/drivers?invite=`
- Company settings tabs gated by permissions (`CompanySettingsTab.tsx`)
- Reuse UI from `frontend/src/components/ui/` (Btn, Inp, Card, etc.)

## Change checklist

1. Add API helper in `api.ts` if new endpoint
2. Gate UI by permission when mutating
3. Manual smoke: one happy path in browser — don't document unless asked

## Do not

- Add new CSS frameworks; use existing inline `G.*` theme tokens
- Fetch with raw fetch outside `api.ts` unless public/unauthenticated route
